WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:14.666
SHOW ONLY THE PA LAYER
In the Explorer, ⊞ on PA scopes every diagram to the physical-architecture package: the components that will be built.

2
00:00:14.666 --> 00:00:27.666
GENERAL VIEW
PA's definitions and usages as boxes: node parts and the behaviour they host, the functions carried over from LA, states, hazards, budgets. Too many to read whole.

3
00:00:27.666 --> 00:00:40.075
READ ONE ELEMENT
Select fleet: the twelve identical drones, multiplicity 12 in Properties. 14 of PA's 21 functions are allocated to it; the ground nodes take the rest.

4
00:00:40.075 --> 00:00:51.872
INTERCONNECTION VIEW
PA's centrepiece: parts with ports, joined by typed physical links. A node part draws the behaviour parts it hosts nested inside its box.

5
00:00:51.872 --> 00:01:04.000
THE GROUND LINKS
The ground station, the recall transmitter and the fleet, port to port. Each line is a connection: taskingFeed, priorityFeed, recallBroadcastFeed…

6
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:15.734
A LINK IS TYPED
Select recallBroadcastFeed in the Explorer. Properties › Types: RecallRadioMedium, a recall radio separate from the mesh and the ground link.

7
00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:29.738
BEHAVIOUR NESTED IN A NODE
Select MissionComputerNode and press Selection. The drone's mission computer hosts four behaviour parts: perception, swarmCoordination, reportHold, directiveUptake.

8
00:01:29.738 --> 00:01:41.528
HOST A PART IN ITS NODE
Before recording we deleted ruleMonitor, the flight-rule monitor that SafetyMonitorNode hosts. Select that node: its box is now empty.

9
00:01:41.528 --> 00:01:54.524
PLACE A PART INSIDE IT
Pick Part in the palette, then click ON the SafetyMonitorNode box. The part is created inside it and the box is redrawn as its host; Selection frames it.

10
00:01:54.524 --> 00:02:06.969
NAME IT AND TYPE IT
In Properties: the name ruleMonitor, then the type FlightRuleMonitor, and Enter binds it. That is all the original had: no documentation of its own.

11
00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:19.962
THE RESULT
The breadcrumb reads PA › SafetyMonitorNode › ruleMonitor, as before we deleted it: the flight rules run apart from the mission computer. Edits stay in this browser.

12
00:02:19.962 --> 00:02:30.951
ACTION VIEW
The 21 functions carried over from LA, each allocated to a component. No successions and no flows between them: a set, not a sequence.

13
00:02:30.951 --> 00:02:43.817
STATE VIEW
Five state machines: a drone's sortie and its operating condition, the ground station's link and duty, the fleet's mesh. The sortie one runs on the safety monitor.

14
00:02:43.817 --> 00:02:56.157
REQUIREMENT VIEW
The six hazards this physical split adds, each satisfied by a component: fleet, the ground station, the recall transmitter, triage, the record store.

15
00:02:56.157 --> 00:03:11.550
PARAMETRIC VIEW
15 constraints: the budgets and two checks on estimates, each with its condition in the box. Select one and zoom in: fleetMemberCount ≤ 12, the fleet is not larger than the twelve the brief fixes.

16
00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:22.961
TREE VIEW
What PA contains, one branch at a time. +N on a box opens what it owns: +4 on MissionComputerNode shows its four behaviour parts.
